---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
import { getSitePage, REVIEWED_DATE, REVIEWED_ISO } from "../data/sitePages";

const page = getSitePage("/terms/");
---

<BaseLayout
  title={page.title}
  description={page.description}
  alternateMd="/terms/index.md"
  pageType="WebPage"
  dateModified={REVIEWED_ISO}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Terms" }]} />
  <section class="tight">
    <div class="wrap narrow prose">
      <h1>Terms of sale and website use</h1>
      <p class="small">Last reviewed: {REVIEWED_DATE}</p>
      <p class="lead" style="font-size:1.05rem;color:var(--ink-2)">
        These terms govern quotations and orders for custom-printed labels, stickers and hang tags from
        {site.company.legalNameEn}. Read them with the written quotation and approved proof.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Definitions</h2>
      <p>
        “Seller”, “we” and “us” mean {site.company.legalNameEn}. “Buyer” and “you” mean the business ordering.
        “Goods” means the printed items. “Artwork” means your files and instructions. “Proof” means the approval
        proof. “Order” means the specification confirmed in writing.
      </p>

      <h2>2. The website is an information service</h2>
      <p>
        This site has no cart, account or checkout. A page, sample request or email template is not an order, and
        browsing creates no contract. Only a written quotation, confirmation and required deposit form an order.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Quotations and their validity</h2>
      <p>
        A quotation applies to its named specification, quantity and destination and is valid for 30 days. Shipping
        terms refer to Incoterms® 2020. A quotation is not a price guarantee for different
        inputs or a different freight route.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Order formation</h2>
      <p>
        An order forms when we confirm it in writing and the deposit clears. The confirmation, quotation, approved
        proof and these terms form the order documents. Production starts after written proof approval and the deposit;
        a purchase-order number or portal entry does not replace our confirmation.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Minimum order quantity</h2>
      <p>
        The minimum is {site.moq} units per design. Designs can share one order where material, size, finish and
        production method match. Changing the quantity may change unit price, packing and lead time, as confirmed in
        the quotation.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Artwork and intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        You confirm you own or are licensed to use every artwork element. You grant a limited licence to reproduce and
        adapt it only to quote, proof, produce and ship the order. We do not resell the design; it remains yours, while
        proofs, dielines and production files remain our working documents. We do not publish your artwork, brand or
        order details without written permission.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Proofs and approval</h2>
      <p>
        Check spelling, dimensions, layout, colour, barcode data, legal text and the dieline before approval. Written
        approval makes the proof the production specification. Colour can vary between screens, proofs and runs; an
        exact match must be agreed in writing. A physical sample can be quoted where surface, adhesion or colour is
        critical.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Prices and taxes</h2>
      <p>
        Prices are in the quotation currency and exclude VAT, import duty, customs fees and destination taxes unless
        the quotation includes them. The shipping term determines who arranges and pays freight, insurance and
        clearance. A change you request after quotation may require a revised price and lead time.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Payment and bank-detail fraud warning</h2>
      <p>
        Payment terms are in the quotation. Production starts after the deposit clears; the balance is due before
        dispatch unless credit is agreed in writing. This website does not take card payments, and banking details
        appear only on the invoice for a confirmed order. <strong>If bank details in an email differ from the invoice,
        call the number on the invoice before paying.</strong> Do not rely on a message that changes an account at the
        last minute. Verify before paying.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Delivery and risk</h2>
      <p>
        Production and transit are separate. Lead times are estimates from proof approval and depend on material,
        capacity, carrier and customs. Risk passes under the Incoterms® 2020 rule in the quotation, or when goods
        leave our premises if no rule is stated. A date is fixed only if confirmed in writing.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Inspection and claims</h2>
      <p>
        Inspect goods on delivery. Report a production defect such as a wrong material, size, print or quantity within
        30 days, and transit damage or a short delivery within 7 days. Include the order number, affected quantity,
        photographs and the batch or lot reference. We may ask for the goods to be retained for inspection and will
        confirm the remedy in writing. For a defect that is ours, you choose a reprint of the affected quantity or a
        refund of it; if a reprint would miss your deadline, we refund instead. Where the goods match the approved
        proof and the fault sits in the artwork, we can reprint at cost price — that is a paid reprint, not a
        warranty claim, and we will say so before you commit.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Warranty</h2>
      <p>
        We warrant that goods materially match the approved proof and specification when they leave us. We do not
        warrant that a label, artwork or claim satisfies the law or is accepted by a retailer, marketplace or
        authority. No other warranty applies beyond mandatory law. Defects from artwork approved as supplied, an
        undisclosed surface or misuse after delivery are excluded.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the extent permitted by law, our total liability for an order is limited to the amount paid for it. We are
        not liable for indirect or consequential loss, lost sales or lost anticipated profit. Nothing excludes liability
        for fraud, death or personal injury caused by negligence, or a right that cannot lawfully be excluded. Mandatory
        consumer rights are preserved.
      </p>

      <h2>14. Force majeure</h2>
      <p>
        A party is not liable for delay caused by an event outside its reasonable control, including carrier
        disruption, customs action or production-partner failure. The affected party will give prompt notice and the
        parties will agree a revised schedule or cancel the unaffected part of the order.
      </p>

      <h2>15. Export control, sanctions and anti-bribery</h2>
      <p>
        You are responsible for the end use and lawful import of the goods. You confirm that no trade sanction
        prohibits the transaction and that the goods are not intended for a prohibited end use. Neither party will
        offer or accept a bribe. We may pause a transaction if a sanctions or export-control check cannot be resolved.
      </p>

      <h2>16. Confidentiality</h2>
      <p>
        Each party will use the other's non-public information only to perform the order and protect it with reasonable
        care. Artwork, customer names and pricing are confidential. We may disclose information where law requires it,
        to an adviser under a duty of confidence, or to a carrier or authority needed for shipment.
      </p>

      <h2>17. Governing law and CISG</h2>
      <p>
        These terms and the order are governed by the laws of the People's Republic of China, excluding conflict-of-law
        rules. The United Nations Convention on Contracts for the International Sale of Goods (CISG) is excluded where
        the parties may exclude it, unless the quotation states otherwise.
      </p>

      <h2>18. Dispute resolution</h2>
      <p>
        The parties will first try in good faith to resolve a dispute through written discussion for 30 days. If it is
        unresolved, the competent court at the seller's place of business has jurisdiction unless mandatory law
        requires another forum. Each party bears its own negotiation costs unless a court orders otherwise.
      </p>

      <h2>19. Entire agreement</h2>
      <p>
        These terms, the quotation, the confirmation and the approved proof are the entire agreement. A statement in an
        email, chat or call not repeated in those documents does not override them. If a provision is unenforceable,
        the rest remains in force.
      </p>

      <h2>20. Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms for future quotations and orders. The version supplied or linked in the quotation or
        confirmation applies unless both parties agree a change in writing. A later change does not alter an order
        retroactively.
      </p>

      <h2>21. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. Company details are on the
        <a href="/about/">about page</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="small">
        Related policies: <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> · <a href="/cookies/">Cookies</a> ·
        <a href="/refund-policy/">Returns</a> · <a href="/shipping-delivery/">Shipping</a> ·
        <a href="/declarations/">Declarations</a> · <a href="/editorial-standards/">Editorial standards</a> ·
        <a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a> · <a href="/corrections/">Corrections</a> ·
        <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> · <a href="/accessibility/">Accessibility</a> ·
        <a href="/contact/">Contact</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
